Container distributions include project LICENSE and NOTICE under
/usr/share/licenses/bartl-restic/. The go/ subdirectory contains license and
NOTICE files collected for the linked controller and worker Go packages by
google/go-licenses v2.0.1. The golang/ subdirectory retains the Go runtime
license and patent notice for those binaries.

The image retains the unmodified Restic binary from its pinned upstream
restic/restic:0.19.1 linux/amd64 container. Its embedded build information
identifies Go 1.26.4, CGO_ENABLED=0 and the build tags selfupdate and
disable_grpc_modules. The restic/ subdirectory contains Restic's license and
dependency notices collected from the corresponding v0.19.1 upstream Go module
using that toolchain, target and build tags, plus the Go runtime notices.
restic-build.txt records the container binary's embedded Go build information.
The Dockerfile pins the exact upstream runtime manifest; it does not replace
the container binary with a separately downloaded release executable.

Upstream base-image license and copyright files remain at their original paths.
The OCI license label identifies the original Bartl code license, not a
relicensing of the complete base image or its third-party components.
